<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xavier Coppolani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a>–<a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xavier Coppolani was a Corsican-born French colonial administrator and scholar of Islamic brotherhoods. From 1902 he pursued a policy of peaceful penetration in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a>, using alliances with religious leaders to bring the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a> of Trarza and Brakna under French protection, until he was assassinated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tijikja">Tidjikja</a> in 1905.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xavier-coppolani.jpg" alt="Xavier Coppolani" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agence Rol · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Xavier_Coppolani.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
